## Overview

This is a **conference-keynote system**, not a website — a 16:9 slide deck from AWS re:Invent 2019 (session **AIM203-S**), co-presented by Intel, Peak and Footasylum. It runs on **two alternating worlds** that give the deck its rhythm:

1. **Brand slides** — full-bleed on the re:Invent **diagonal gradient** (`{colors.grad-blue}` → `{colors.grad-magenta}` → `{colors.grad-orange}` → `{colors.grad-lavender}`), sliced by a hard diagonal seam. These carry the session code, big section titles, partner logo lockups and the standard AWS footer. Used for the cover, every section divider, and the Q&A / Thank-you closers.
2. **Content slides** — a warm near-black charcoal (`{colors.canvas-dark}`) with a **light-weight Amazon Ember** headline top-left and a flat body of icon rows, three-up comparisons, timelines and charts. A handful of "product screenshot" slides invert to white (`{colors.canvas-light}`).

Type is **Amazon Ember** throughout, and the signature is the **weight contrast**: a thin 300 headline against 400 body, with 700 reserved for names, labels, stat numerals and the section-bold gradient titles.

The deck tells one repeating story — **Context / Convenience / Control** — and hard-codes it into a **three-color accent system**: mint, coral, cyan. The same trio doubles as Marketing / Merchandising / Supply chain, and as the Customer AI / Demand AI / Supply AI product pillars. On top of that, the **Peak AI System diagrams** introduce a second palette (lime green, magenta, yellow, violet) that codes architecture *layers* rather than the narrative.

**Key characteristics:**
- Everything is **flat** — no drop shadows anywhere. Depth comes from the gradient, from full-bleed photography, and from color-block contrast.
- **Light 300 headlines** set top-left, consistently, on every content slide.
- The **Context/Convenience/Control** trio (mint/coral/cyan) is the connective tissue — carried by dots, chips, underlines and icon accents.
- **Huge 700 numerals** (`28%`, `10x`, `+4%`, `30%`) are the primary "proof" device.
- Section-divider slides always sit on the **re:Invent gradient**; content always drops to **charcoal**. The alternation is the pacing.
- Icons are **thin single-weight line icons**, white on dark.
- The **Peak logo** (P-E / A-K glyph) top-right marks every Peak-authored content slide; the **AWS smile + re:Invent logo** anchor gradient slides.

