## Typography

### Font family
The system runs **Amazon Ember** — the AWS corporate typeface — for everything. Fallback stack: `system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif`.

The weight split is the signature:
- **Ember Light (300)** → all slide headlines, hero titles, presenter roles
- **Ember Regular (400)** → body bullets, captions, subheads, footer
- **Ember Bold (700)** → session code, section-divider titles, stat numerals, presenter names, diagram labels, emphasis lead-ins

### Hierarchy

| Token | Size | Weight | Tracking | Use |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `{typography.display-hero}` | 96px | 300 | 0 | "Q&A", "Thank you!" giant covers |
| `{typography.display-section-bold}` | 60px | 700 | 0 | Gradient section dividers ("The AI tech stack for retail", "AI Infrastructure", "AI Studio", "Peak solutions") |
| `{typography.display-title-slide}` | 52px | 300 | 0 | Cover-slide title ("Take AI/ML from theory to practice…") |
| `{typography.heading-slide}` | 40px | 300 | 0 | Every content-slide headline, top-left |
| `{typography.stat-numeral}` | 120px | 700 | −1px | Big proof numbers ("28%", "10x", "30%", "+4%") |
| `{typography.stat-caption}` | 26px | 400 | 0 | Line under a stat ("Uplift in email revenue") |
| `{typography.presenter-name}` | 26px | 700 | 0 | "Richard Potter", "Tom Summerfield" |
| `{typography.presenter-role}` | 22px | 300 | 0 | "CEO / Peak", role + org lines |
| `{typography.subhead-accent}` | 22px | 400 | 0 | Mint accent subheads under a title |
| `{typography.body-bullet}` | 24px | 400 | 0 | Agenda items, bullet body |
| `{typography.body-caption-label}` | 22px | 400 | 0 | Icon-row captions ("Context", "Convenience"…) |
| `{typography.session-code}` | 18px | 700 | 6px | "A I M 2 0 3 - S" eyebrow |
| `{typography.diagram-label}` | 15px | 700 | 0.3px | "Customer AI", "AI Studio", box labels |
| `{typography.footer-legal}` | 11px | 400 | 0.2px | Copyright footer |

### Principles
- **Light headline, regular body, bold numerals** — the three-weight rhythm is fixed. Avoid medium (500); it isn't in the system.
- **Wide-tracked uppercase** is reserved for the **session code** (6px) and the **section chips** — the "conference badge" voice.
- Titles **always sit top-left** on content slides; gradient-divider titles sit **left-center**.
- **Numerals do the persuading.** When there's a metric, it's set enormous in 700 with a small regular caption beneath and a thin rule.

### Note on font substitutes
Amazon Ember is licensed to Amazon and not freely distributable. Close open-source stand-ins:
- **Inter** — near match; run 300 / 400 / 700 and leave tracking at 0.
- **Ember-alikes**: "Public Sans" or "Source Sans 3" for a slightly warmer body.
- Keep the **Light/Regular/Bold** trio and the wide-tracked uppercase eyebrow to preserve the feel.

## Layout

### Canvas & margins
- **Frame:** 16:9 (1280×720 / 1920×1080).
- **Slide margin:** ~`{spacing.slide-margin}` (72px) on content slides; title sits in the top-left corner within that margin.
- **Base unit:** 8px; steps `{spacing.xxs}` 4 · `{spacing.xs}` 8 · `{spacing.sm}` 12 · `{spacing.md}` 16 · `{spacing.lg}` 24 · `{spacing.xl}` 40 · `{spacing.xxl}` 64.

### Recurring layouts
- **Title top-left + content below/right** — the default content slide.
- **Split slide** — text left on charcoal, product screenshot right on white (We are Footasylum, The Peak AI System).
- **Three-up icon triad** — three centered columns, icon → thin colored rule → caption. The mint/coral/cyan trio colors the rule or the dot.
- **Timeline row** — three icons across the top, dropped stems to a dotted horizontal line, mint/coral/cyan dots at each node ("Connected retail isn't easy").
- **Prediction + Optimization = Profitability** — the pillar slides: data-cloud icons far left → product UI mock → a bracketed list of capabilities → an "=" → an outcomes list. A colored section chip pins the top-right.
- **Left value-stack ↔ right system diagram** — the Peak "Outcomes / Solutions / Workflow / Infrastructure / Data" stack mirrored against the boxed AI System architecture.
- **Gradient divider** — full-bleed gradient, big 700 title left-center, partner logos top-left, AWS + re:Invent marks bottom corners.

### Whitespace philosophy
Content slides are **generous and airy** — one idea per slide, a lot of charcoal breathing room around a single triad or diagram. The density only rises inside the **product UI screenshots** and the **Peak architecture diagram**, which are intentionally detailed.

## Elevation & Depth

| Level | Treatment | Use |
|---|---|---|
| Flat | No shadow, no border | Titles, body, icon rows, timelines |
| Gradient field | Full-bleed re:Invent gradient | Covers, dividers, closers |
| Full-bleed photo | Edge-to-edge imagery (storefront, city, crowd) | Chapter openers, "Delivering connected retail" |
| Color block | Solid mint/coral/cyan chip or violet/navy stat block over photo | Section labels, proof numbers |
| Outline box | 1px white/green/yellow stroke | Peak AI System architecture frame + cards |
| Faux UI card | Light-grey browser chrome, `{rounded.md}` | Product screenshots (AI System login, Workflow, dashboards) |

The deck **never uses a drop shadow.** Depth is entirely gradient + photography + color-block contrast + the occasional 1px outline.

### Decorative accents
- **Stitched / hatch texture** — a small green cross-hatch (`{colors.stitch-green}`) tucked under stat blocks and beside Peak flow steps.
- **Dotted connector lines** — thin dotted rules link timeline nodes and pipeline steps.
- **Concentric ring motif** — dashed rings radiating from a phone on the closing "connected retail" photo slide.

## Shapes

### Corner radius

| Token | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `{rounded.none}` | 0px | Section chips, stat blocks, Peak architecture boxes, pillar-label navy bars — the dominant radius |
| `{rounded.card}` | 6px | Faux browser UI window corners |
| `{rounded.md}` | 8px | UI mock frames, rare rounded panels |
| `{rounded.full}` | 50% | Timeline dots, numbered circles, icon-accent dots, the round Peak logo badge |

The radius logic is **binary**, like BMW's: **rectangular for every box and chip; circular only for dots, numbered markers and the Peak badge.** UI screenshots are the one place softer corners appear.

### Photography geometry
- Full-bleed 16:9 chapter photos (storefronts, crowds, city skyline).
- **Skewed/parallelogram photo tiles** — the "Retailers need to be better connected" images are cut on a slight 3D skew, each pinned with a numbered mint/coral/cyan circle.
- Circular photo crops (paired overlapping circles on "We are Footasylum") with a green connective shape between them.

## Components

### Session-code eyebrow
**`session-code-eyebrow`** — the "A I M 2 0 3 - S" label. `{typography.session-code}` (18px / 700 / **6px tracking**, uppercase), white, top-left above the title on cover and divider slides.

### Titles & subheads
**`slide-title`** — top-left, `{typography.heading-slide}` (40px / 300), white on charcoal.
**`slide-subhead`** — the mint accent line beneath it, `{typography.subhead-accent}` (22px / 400) in `{colors.accent-mint}` ("With customers", "… and internally too", "An intelligence layer across the enterprise").

### Section chips
**`section-chip-context` / `-convenience` / `-control`** — top-right rectangular chips (0px radius) on the pillar slides. Fill is the lightened accent (`chip-*-bg`), text is dark navy `{colors.chip-label-ink}`, uppercase bold. These name which of the three Cs the slide belongs to.

### Agenda list
**`agenda-numeral`** — numbers `1.`–`7.` in `{colors.accent-mint}`, items in white `{typography.body-bullet}`, generous line spacing, paired with a full-bleed skewed photo on the right half.

### Icon triads
**`icon-triad-column`** — three centered columns: thin white line icon → short colored rule (`accent-mint` / `accent-coral` / `accent-cyan`, or grey) → caption in `{typography.body-caption-label}`. Used on "MLOps in a box", "Enterprise-grade security", "in practice" slides.

### Timeline / pipeline
**`timeline-dot-connector`** — icons across the top, thin stems dropping to a **dotted horizontal line**, with the mint/coral/cyan **dots** at each node. Bold captions below, colored metric sub-captions ("1m+ consumers", "25k products", "Omnichannel fulfillment").
**`pipeline-flow-row`** — left-to-right flow of tech marks (streaming → Apache Spark → S3/Redshift → AI/ML gear) joined by dotted separators, each with a stem-and-tick and a caption.

### Stat blocks
**`stat-numeral-block`** — a giant `{typography.stat-numeral}` (120px / 700) in `{colors.accent-mint}` with a small regular caption and a thin white rule beneath ("28% — Uplift in email revenue", "10x — Return on Ad spend").
**`stat-block-on-photo`** — over the NYC skyline, solid **violet** (`{colors.stat-violet}`) and **navy** (`{colors.stat-navy}`) rectangles hold "30% faster" / "50% higher profit margins" in white.

### Peak AI System diagram
**`peak-system-frame`** — an outlined "AI System" box containing a top row of four cards + two full-width layer bars, wired below to a dashed "Systems of record / engagement / Data warehouse" group.
**`peak-solution-card`** / **`-active`** — the four cards (Customer AI, Demand AI, Supply AI, Data Studio). Idle = thin outline (green for the three AIs, magenta for Data Studio); active = **filled** green / magenta with dark text. Progressive slides light these up step by step.
**`peak-layer-highlight`** — the **AI Studio** and **AI Infrastructure** bars flip to solid **yellow** (`{colors.peak-yellow}`) to spotlight that layer in the numbered walkthrough (1 → 2 → 3).
Left mirror stack: **Outcomes** (violet) / Solutions (green) / Workflow / Infrastructure / Data, connected by UML-style ball-and-socket connectors.

### Product UI mocks
**`ui-mock-browser-frame`** — light-grey browser chrome with traffic-light dots and a `{rounded.md}` window, holding real-looking Peak screens (login, workflow DAG, Customer AI dashboard with metric tiles and bar charts). Charts inside use magenta / navy / violet bars and a green trend line.

### Charts
**`chart-line`** — dual line charts on charcoal: **pink** UK line + **yellow** US line, quiet grey grid and axis labels, a bold accent metric callout beside each ("+4% YoY growth" in pink, "+3%" in yellow) and a muted source note.

### Presenter block & logo lockup
**`presenter-block`** — name in `{typography.presenter-name}` (26px / 700), role + org in `{typography.presenter-role}` (300). Two side-by-side on shared-title slides.
**`partner-logo-lockup`** — white partner logos separated by a thin vertical `{colors.ink-on-dark-soft}` divider (PEAK | aws | intel), top area of gradient dividers.

