**`slide-footer`** — centered "© 2019, Amazon Web Services, Inc. or its affiliates. All rights reserved." in `{typography.footer-legal}`, flanked by the re:Invent mark (bottom-left) and AWS smile (bottom-right) on gradient slides.

## Do's and Don'ts

### Do
- Reserve the **re:Invent gradient** for covers, section dividers and closers; drop to `{colors.canvas-dark}` charcoal for all content.
- Keep the **Context = mint / Convenience = coral / Control = cyan** mapping consistent everywhere — dots, chips, underlines, icon accents.
- Set headlines in **Ember Light 300, top-left**; body in Regular 400; reserve 700 for numerals, names, chips and diagram labels.
- Make metrics **huge** (120px, 700) with a small caption and a thin rule — the deck's core proof device.
- Keep icons **thin, single-weight, white** on dark.
- Light up the **Peak diagram layer by layer** (green cards, yellow Studio/Infra, magenta Data Studio, violet Outcomes) to walk the architecture.
- Mark Peak content slides with the **PEAK glyph top-right**; mark gradient slides with **AWS + re:Invent**.

### Don't
- Don't add drop shadows — the system is flat; depth is gradient + photo + color block.
- Don't introduce a fourth "narrative" accent beyond mint/coral/cyan; the Peak green/yellow/magenta/violet set is for **architecture layers only**, not the three-Cs story.
- Don't set headlines bold — 300 Light is the headline voice; bold is for numerals and labels.
- Don't center body content — titles and copy anchor **top-left / left**.
- Don't run two gradient slides back-to-back for content; gradient is punctuation, charcoal is the body.
- Don't tighten tracking on body; save wide letter-spacing for the **session code** and **chips**.
- Don't recolor the section chips off their C — Context stays mint, Convenience coral, Control cyan.

