## Known Gaps
- **Amazon Ember** and **Peak's** brand fonts/marks are proprietary; Inter (300/400/700) is the documented substitute.
- Exact gradient stop positions and the diagonal seam angle are approximate — sampled visually, not from source vectors.
- Hex values are eyedropped from rendered slides; treat them as close matches, not brand-exact tokens.
- Animation/build order (the card-by-card Peak diagram reveals) is inferred from the static sequence; timing is out of scope.
- Semantic colors (success/warning/error) are inferred from the accent set — the deck doesn't use explicit form/UI states.
- The product UI screenshots imply a separate Peak web-app design language (light theme, its own component set) that isn't fully captured here.
